# Advisories the vulnerability scan is told to skip.
#
# Empty on purpose. Every advisory Trivy reports today has a released fix and has been
# taken, so nothing needs suppressing.
#
# Add an entry only when the advisory cannot be fixed, not when fixing it is inconvenient.
# That is roughly two cases: no fixed version exists yet, or the vulnerable code path is
# provably unreachable from Ingot. "The bump breaks something" is a reason to fix the
# breakage, not to hide the advisory.
#
# Record the reason and an expiry date, so a suppression that outlived its cause shows up
# instead of sitting here forever:
#
#   # netty's HTTP/3 codec is not on our classpath; the advisory is unreachable.
#   CVE-0000-00000 exp:2026-12-31
#
# The scan itself lives in .github/workflows/ci.yml and fails on CRITICAL, HIGH and MEDIUM.
